      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The injection of the small-fibre excitant and inflammatory irritant mustard oil (MO) into the temporomandibular joint (TMJ) region of rats evokes a sustained and reversible increase in electromyographic (EMG) activity of jaw muscles. The 'rekindling' of this nociceptive reflex by intrathecal (i.t.) administration of the opiate antagonist naloxone and mu but not delta and kappa selective opioid antagonist, suggests that it may be modulated by endogenous opioid inhibitory mechanisms."},
